/-!
# Zariski descent for modules on the affine opens of a scheme

Let `X` be a scheme and let `M` be a presheaf of modules on the site `X.affineOpens` of affine
opens of `X` over the restriction of the structure sheaf, and suppose `M` is **cartesian**: for
every inclusion `V ≤ U` of affine opens the base-change comparison
`M(U) ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(X, V) ⟶ M(V)` is an isomorphism. This file proves that `M` then satisfies
the sheaf condition for the Zariski topology `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.affineOpensTopology`.

This is the implication (1) ⟹ (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0GZX] for the Zariski topology on a scheme, in
the part which asserts the sheaf property; it is also the step of the source's proof of the
comparison (3) ≃ (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0GZZ] which lists "the sheaf property for the Zariski
topology" among its four conditions.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isSheaf_affineOpensTopology_of_cartesian` — **a cartesian presheaf of
  modules on the affine opens of a scheme is a Zariski sheaf.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isSheafFor_ofArrows_affineBasicOpen` — the sheaf axiom for a finite
  family of basic opens of an affine open whose sections generate the unit ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_spanning_basicOpen_family` — **a Zariski covering sieve of an
  affine open is refined by a finite family of basic opens generating the unit ideal**, which is
  quasi-compactness of an affine scheme in the form the descent argument consumes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isPushout_presheaf_map_basicOpen` — for `a b : Γ(X, U)` with `U` affine the
  square of restriction maps attached to `X.basicOpen a`, `X.basicOpen b` and their intersection
  is a pushout of rings, i.e. `Γ(X, D(a) ⊓ D(b)) = Γ(X, D(a)) ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(X, D(b))`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.faithfullyFlat_pi_presheaf_map_basicOpen` — the product of the restriction
  maps of a family of basic opens generating the unit ideal is faithfully flat.

## The shape of the argument, and why basic opens

The engine is `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheafFor_of_cartesian`, descent of modules along a
faithfully flat ring map read on a site: it asks for a finite covering family whose rings of
sections are faithfully flat over the base and whose double overlaps make the ring square a
pushout. Its companion
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/CartesianModulesOnAffineSite.lean` feeds it a site of
affine *schemes with pullbacks*, which the poset of affine opens is not; the overlaps there are
fibre products and the pushout comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPushout_appTop_of_isPullback`.

Here the covering family is refined to **basic opens** of the affine open being covered, and that
removes every trace of scheme geometry from the two ring-theoretic inputs:

* the double overlap of `D(a)` and `D(b)` is `D(a|_{D(b)})`, a basic open of `D(b)`, so the
  pushout is the base change of a localization away from one element and is
  `CategoryTheory.CommRingCat.isPushout_of_isLocalization`;
* `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(X, D(a))` is that localization, hence flat, and the product over a family
  generating the unit ideal is surjective on spectra because a prime cannot contain the whole
  family — so `RingHom.FaithfullyFlat.pi` applies.

Refining to basic opens costs nothing because a sieve is closed under precomposition: a basic
open contained in a member of the sieve is itself a member. The refinement is produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.exists_basicOpen_le` at each point and cut down to a finite
family by `Ideal.span_eq_top_iff_finite`, through
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff`.

Passing from the covering family to an arbitrary covering sieve is
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheafFor_subsieve`, which asks for the sheaf axiom on every pullback
of the refining sieve. In a poset the pullback of the sieve generated by a family of opens along
an inclusion `V' ≤ U` is the sieve generated by the intersections, and the intersection of `V'`
with `D(a)` is the basic open `D(a|_{V'})`; so the pullbacks are again families of basic opens,
and the restricted sections still generate the unit ideal. That bookkeeping is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.mem_generate_ofArrows_affineOpens_iff`, which identifies the sieve
generated by a family of affine opens with "being contained in one of them".

## Implementation notes

The structure presheaf is written `X.affineOpensToOpens.op ⋙ X.presheaf` rather than
`X.affineZariskiRingedSite.O.obj`. The two are the same term, but with the second one the
underlying category of the site is a projection `RingedSite.C` on which instance search cannot
find the order on the affine opens, so `homOfLE` does not elaborate.

Several goals mix the two spellings `Γ(X, ↑(X.affineBasicOpen a))` and `Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)` of
one type; they are definitionally equal but not syntactically so, so `rw` refuses the goals that
contain both and the inequalities are proved at the `X.Opens` level and transported by `exact`,
as in `AlgebraicGeometry.flat_presheaf_map_of_isAffineOpen`.

